From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:32:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 301/342] meson_dwmac: a sender that waited takes the slot free
 by then

Write() chose its slot once, before waiting for room in the ring without the lock,
and used it afterwards. Two senders waiting together both had the same slot: the
second overwrote it and moved the position on past the next slot, which was never
filled, and the transmit engine rightly stopped there for good. That's the ring seen
at the stalls: the slot behind the engine still owned, the one at the engine not,
with the length of its last frame still there. My reading of that as a frame status
closing the wrong descriptor was wrong. Found by a review of this code with Codex.

Three TCP streams and pings both ways before this, without operate on second frame:
25 stalls in two rounds of 24 s, and the link gone in the second.

The count of senders overtaken this way is shown with the other state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../network/ether/meson_dwmac/meson_dwmac.cpp | 46 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/meson_dwmac/meson_dwmac.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/meson_dwmac/meson_dwmac.cpp
index 2f53bcad29..e263475580 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/meson_dwmac/meson_dwmac.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/meson_dwmac/meson_dwmac.cpp
@@ -323,6 +323,7 @@ private:
 			sem_id				fLinkStateSemaphore;
 
 			int32				fTxStuckSeconds;
+			int32				fTxSendersOvertaken;
 			bool				fSecondFrame;
 };
 
@@ -357,6 +358,7 @@ MesonDwmac::MesonDwmac(device_node* node)
 	fSpeed(0),
 	fLinkStateSemaphore(-1),
 	fTxStuckSeconds(0),
+	fTxSendersOvertaken(0),
 	fSecondFrame(true)
 {
 	memset(fMacAddress, 0, sizeof(fMacAddress));
@@ -694,14 +696,21 @@ MesonDwmac::Write(const void* buffer, size_t* _length)
 
 	MutexLocker locker(fTxLock);
 
-	uint32 slot = fTxHead;
-	volatile descriptor* desc = _TxDescriptor(slot);
-	_SyncDescriptor(kRxCount + slot, true);
-	while ((desc->status & DESC_OWN) != 0) {
-		// the ring is full: wait for the DMA engine (the timeout also covers
-		// a lost interrupt)
+	// The slot is the one at the driver's position when there's room: another
+	// sender can move that on while this one waits without the lock.
+	uint32 slot;
+	volatile descriptor* desc;
+	while (true) {
 		if (!fOpen)
 			return B_FILE_ERROR;
+		slot = fTxHead;
+		desc = _TxDescriptor(slot);
+		_SyncDescriptor(kRxCount + slot, true);
+		if ((desc->status & DESC_OWN) == 0)
+			break;
+
+		// the ring is full: wait for the DMA engine (the timeout also covers
+		// a lost interrupt)
 		if (fNonBlocking)
 			return B_WOULD_BLOCK;
 		ConditionVariableEntry entry;
@@ -715,10 +724,10 @@ MesonDwmac::Write(const void* buffer, size_t* _length)
 		locker.Lock();
 		if (waitStatus != B_OK && waitStatus != B_TIMED_OUT)
 			return waitStatus;
-		_SyncDescriptor(kRxCount + slot, true);
+
+		if (fTxHead != slot)
+			atomic_add(&fTxSendersOvertaken, 1);
 	}
-	if (!fOpen)
-		return B_FILE_ERROR;
 
 	status_t status = user_memcpy(_Buffer(kRxCount + slot), buffer, length);
 	if (status != B_OK)
@@ -899,15 +908,13 @@ MesonDwmac::_ConfigureEee()
 }
 
 
-/*!	The transmit engine can stay suspended with frames waiting, whatever the
-	poll demands say: the slot behind its position is still its own, the one at
-	its position has lost OWN with its length intact, as if a frame's status had
-	closed the next descriptor. It happened within a few GB without OPERATION_OSF,
-	and with it once in about 110 GB.
+/*!	A safety net: the transmit engine suspended for 2 s with frames waiting,
+	which no poll demand will change if a slot among them isn't its own. Write()
+	used to leave such a hole, when two senders had waited for the same slot.
 
-	After 2 s of that, gives the ring back to the engine in order, from the
-	oldest frame. A frame that had gone out may go out again, which TCP copes
-	with, and which nothing else on a LAN minds much.
+	Gives the ring back to the engine in order, from the oldest frame. A frame
+	that had gone out may go out again, which TCP copes with, and which nothing
+	else on a LAN minds much.
 */
 void
 MesonDwmac::_CheckTransmit()
@@ -1005,8 +1012,9 @@ MesonDwmac::DumpState(void (*print)(const char*, ...))
 		}
 	}
 	print("meson_dwmac: received %" B_PRIu32 " frames, %" B_PRIu32
-		" CRC errors, missed %#" B_PRIx32 "\n", _Read(kMmcRxFrames),
-		_Read(kMmcRxCrcErrors), _Read(kDmaMissedFrames));
+		" CRC errors, missed %#" B_PRIx32 "; senders overtaken while waiting: %"
+		B_PRId32 "\n", _Read(kMmcRxFrames), _Read(kMmcRxCrcErrors),
+		_Read(kDmaMissedFrames), fTxSendersOvertaken);
 }
 
 
